    {
      "level": 2,
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "Background and motivation",
          "marks": [],
          "type": "Text"
        }
      ],
      "numbered": true,
      "label": null,
      "type": "Section"
    },
    {
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "The report class is the natural choice for any long-form document with chapters: theses, dissertations, technical reports, and project write-ups. It differs from the article class mainly in that Heading 1 produces \\chapter (starting a new page) rather than \\section.",
          "marks": [],
          "type": "Text"
        }
      ],
      "alignment": "justify",
      "type": "Paragraph"
    },
    {
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "Recent advances in the field ",
          "marks": [],
          "type": "Text"
        },
        {
          "keys": [
            "smith2020",
            "jones2021"
          ],
          "style": "citep",
          "type": "Citation"
        },
        {
          "text": " have opened new avenues for exploration. However, several open questions remain, particularly concerning the scalability of existing approaches and their applicability to real-world datasets.",
          "marks": [],
          "type": "Text"
        }
      ],
      "alignment": "justify",
      "type": "Paragraph"
    },
    {
      "level": 2,
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "Research objectives",
          "marks": [],
          "type": "Text"
        }
      ],
      "numbered": true,
      "label": null,
      "type": "Section"
    },
    {
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "This thesis addresses the following research questions:",
          "marks": [],
          "type": "Text"
        }
      ],
      "alignment": "justify",
      "type": "Paragraph"
    },
    {
      "ordered": true,
      "items": [
        {
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "How does the proposed method compare to baseline approaches on standard benchmarks?",
              "marks": [],
              "type": "Text"
            }
          ],
          "type": "ListItem"
        },
        {
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "What is the computational complexity of the algorithm, and how does it scale with input size?",
              "marks": [],
              "type": "Text"
            }
          ],
          "type": "ListItem"
        },
        {
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "Can the method generalise to unseen domains without re-training?",
              "marks": [],
              "type": "Text"
            }
          ],
          "type": "ListItem"
        }
      ],
      "type": "List"
    },
    {
      "level": 2,
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "Thesis outline",
          "marks": [],
          "type": "Text"
        }
      ],
      "numbered": true,
      "label": null,
      "type": "Section"
    },
    {
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "The remainder of this thesis is organised as follows. Chapter 2 reviews the relevant literature. Chapter 3 describes the methodology and algorithm design. Chapter 4 presents the experimental results (see Table ",
          "marks": [],
          "type": "Text"
        },
        {
          "label": "tab:results",
          "kind": "ref",
          "type": "CrossRef"
        },
        {
          "text": " and Figure ",
          "marks": [],
          "type": "Text"
        },
        {
          "label": "fig:results",
          "kind": "ref",
          "type": "CrossRef"
        },
        {
          "text": "). Chapter 5 discusses the findings, and Chapter 6 concludes with a summary and directions for future work.",
          "marks": [],
          "type": "Text"
        }
      ],
      "alignment": "justify",
      "type": "Paragraph"
    },
    {
      "level": 1,
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "Literature Review",
          "marks": [],
          "type": "Text"
        }
      ],
      "numbered": true,
      "label": null,
      "type": "Section"
    },
    {
      "level": 2,
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "Theoretical foundations",
          "marks": [],
          "type": "Text"
        }
      ],
      "numbered": true,
      "label": null,
      "type": "Section"
    },
    {
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "The mathematical framework underpinning this work builds on the seminal contributions of ",
          "marks": [],
          "type": "Text"
        },
        {
          "keys": [
            "fourier1822"
          ],
          "style": "citet",
          "type": "Citation"
        },
        {
          "text": " and subsequent extensions by ",
          "marks": [],
          "type": "Text"
        },
        {
          "keys": [
            "shannon1948"
          ],
          "style": "citet",
          "type": "Citation"
        },
        {
          "text": ". The key insight is that any signal can be decomposed into a linear combination of orthogonal basis functions.",
          "marks": [],
          "type": "Text"
        }
      ],
      "alignment": "justify",
      "type": "Paragraph"
    },
    {
      "level": 2,
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "Related work",
          "marks": [],
          "type": "Text"
        }
      ],
      "numbered": true,
      "label": null,
      "type": "Section"
    },
    {
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "Several authors have proposed methods that are related to ours. ",
          "marks": [],
          "type": "Text"
        },
        {
          "keys": [
            "doe2019"
          ],
          "style": "citet",
          "type": "Citation"
        },
        {
          "text": " introduced a variational approach that achieves competitive accuracy but requires cubic time complexity. ",
          "marks": [],
          "type": "Text"
        },
        {
          "keys": [
            "lee2022"
          ],
          "style": "citet",
          "type": "Citation"
        },
        {
          "text": " later improved upon this with a linearised approximation, though at the cost of reduced precision.",
          "marks": [],
          "type": "Text"
        }
      ],
      "alignment": "justify",
      "type": "Paragraph"
    },
    {
      "level": 2,
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "Identified gap",
          "marks": [],
          "type": "Text"
        }
      ],
      "numbered": true,
      "label": null,
      "type": "Section"
    },
    {
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "Despite these advances, no existing method simultaneously achieves sub-quadratic complexity and maintains accuracy above 90\\% on the benchmark suite. This thesis proposes a novel algorithm that meets both criteria (see Equation ",
          "marks": [],
          "type": "Text"
        },
        {
          "label": "eq:objective",
          "kind": "eqref",
          "type": "CrossRef"
        },
        {
          "text": " in Chapter 3).",
          "marks": [],
          "type": "Text"
        }
      ],
      "alignment": "justify",
      "type": "Paragraph"
    },
    {
      "level": 1,
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "Methodology",
          "marks": [],
          "type": "Text"
        }
      ],
      "numbered": true,
      "label": null,
      "type": "Section"
    },
    {
      "level": 2,
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "Problem formulation",
          "marks": [],
          "type": "Text"
        }
      ],
      "numbered": true,
      "label": null,
      "type": "Section"
    },
    {
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "Let the input data be represented as a matrix ",
          "marks": [],
          "type": "Text"
        },
        {
          "latex": "X \\in \\mathbb{R}^{n \\times d}",
          "type": "MathInline"
        },
        {
          "text": " and the target vector as ",
          "marks": [],
          "type": "Text"
        },
        {
          "latex": "y \\in \\mathbb{R}^n",
          "type": "MathInline"
        },
        {
          "text": ". The objective is to find the parameter vector ",
          "marks": [],
          "type": "Text"
        },
        {
          "latex": "\\beta^*",
          "type": "MathInline"
        },
        {
          "text": " that minimises the regularised loss:",
          "marks": [],
          "type": "Text"
        }
      ],
      "alignment": "justify",
      "type": "Paragraph"
    },
    {
      "latex": "\\beta^* = \\arg\\min_{\\beta} \\|X\\beta - y\\|_2^2 + \\lambda \\|\\beta\\|_1",
      "numbered": true,
      "label": "eq:objective",
      "type": "MathBlock"
    },
    {
      "level": 2,
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "Proposed algorithm",
          "marks": [],
          "type": "Text"
        }
      ],
      "numbered": true,
      "label": null,
      "type": "Section"
    },
    {
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "We introduce Algorithm 1 below, which solves Equation ",
          "marks": [],
          "type": "Text"
        },
        {
          "label": "eq:objective",
          "kind": "eqref",
          "type": "CrossRef"
        },
        {
          "text": " in ",
          "marks": [],
          "type": "Text"
        },
        {
          "latex": "O(n \\log n)",
          "type": "MathInline"
        },
        {
          "text": " time.",
          "marks": [],
          "type": "Text"
        }
      ],
      "alignment": "justify",
      "type": "Paragraph"
    },
    {
      "text": "\\begin{algorithm}[H]\n\\SetAlgoLined\n\\KwIn{Data matrix $X$, target $y$, regularisation $\\lambda$}\n\\KwOut{Optimal parameters $\\beta^*$}\nInitialise $\\beta_0 \\leftarrow 0$\\;\n\\For{$t = 1$ \\KwTo $T$}{\n  Compute gradient $g_t \\leftarrow \\nabla L(\\beta_{t-1})$\\;\n  Update $\\beta_t \\leftarrow \\mathrm{prox}_{\\lambda}(\\beta_{t-1} - \\eta g_t)$\\;\n}\n\\Return $\\beta_T$\\;\n\\caption{Proximal gradient descent}\n\\label{alg:pgd}\n\\end{algorithm}",
      "type": "RawLatex"
    },
    {
      "level": 2,
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "Implementation details",
          "marks": [],
          "type": "Text"
        }
      ],
      "numbered": true,
      "label": null,
      "type": "Section"
    },
    {
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "The algorithm was implemented in Python 3.12 using NumPy for linear algebra operations. All experiments were run on a workstation with an AMD Ryzen 9 CPU and 64 GB RAM. The convergence tolerance was set to ",
          "marks": [],
          "type": "Text"
        },
        {
          "latex": "\\epsilon = 10^{-6}",
          "type": "MathInline"
        },
        {
          "text": " and the maximum number of iterations to ",
          "marks": [],
          "type": "Text"
        },
        {
          "latex": "T = 10{,}000",
          "type": "MathInline"
        },
        {
          "text": ".",
          "marks": [],
          "type": "Text"
        }
      ],
      "alignment": "justify",
      "type": "Paragraph"
    },
